# Access requests and grants (LWS 1.0 core section 11).
"@context":
  - ../context.jsonld
  - ../touchstone.jsonld
id: "#manifest"
type: Manifest
label: "LWS 1.0 core: access requests and grants"
comment: >-
  Section 11 is optional: a storage MAY advertise AccessRequestService and
  AccessGrantService endpoints. Where it does, a storage controller POSTs an AccessGrant
  and the server "adjusts any underlying access policy". That is also the only
  spec-defined way to give a resource the public or authenticated-agent access that
  lws-test-suite modelled as prerequisites, so its public-read tests live here. When the
  storage advertises no such service, ${service.*} is unresolvable and the test is
  inapplicable; a grant step marked precondition covers servers that advertise the
  service but refuse the grant shape (public access via foaf:Agent is a MAY).
specification:
  - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/
entries:

  - id: "#access-grant-endpoint-is-container"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: access-grant-endpoint-is-container
    label: The access grant endpoint is an LWS container
    comment: >-
      "The access request and access grant endpoints are LWS containers and MUST conform
      to the rules defined in this specification."
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#access-protocol
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#access-discovery
    traits: [Get, AccessGrants, Container]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/access-endpoints-are-lws-containers
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/access-services-advertised
    request:
      method: GET
      url: "${service.AccessGrantService}"
      accept: application/lws+json
    response:
      statusCode: 200
      contentType: application/lws+json
      linkHeaders:
        - rel: type
          href: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws#Container
      json:
        - pointer: /items
          jsonType: array

  - id: "#access-grant-create"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: access-grant-create
    label: A storage controller creates an access grant with POST and reads it back
    comment: >-
      "A successful POST operation MUST respond with a Location header set to the URL of
      the new resource", and the grant is then a readable AccessGrant scoped to the
      storage.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#access-protocol
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#access-data-model
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#odrl-assignee
    traits: [Post, Get, AccessGrants]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/access-post-location-header
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/access-endpoints-jsonld-payloads
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/access-type-values
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/access-storage-uri
    steps:
      - label: grant bob read access to the test container
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.AccessGrantService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            type: [AccessGrant]
            storage: "${storage}"
            access:
              - type: [AccessPolicy]
                action: [read]
                assignee: "${identity.bob.webid}"
                target:
                  type: StorageResource
                  value: ["${test.container}"]
        response:
          statusCode: 201
          location:
            capture: grant
            cleanup: true
      - label: the grant reads back as an AccessGrant for this storage
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${grant}"
          accept: application/lws+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          contentType: application/lws+json
          json:
            - pointer: /type
              hasValue: AccessGrant
            - pointer: /storage
              equalsIri: "${storage}"
            - pointer: /access
              jsonType: array

  - id: "#access-grant-revoke"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: access-grant-revoke
    label: Deleting an access grant withdraws the access it gave
    comment: >-
      DELETE on a grant is RECOMMENDED, and revoking one obliges the server to adjust the
      policy it put in place. Uses a public grant so the effect is visible to an
      anonymous client.
    status: Proposed
    level: SHOULD
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#access-protocol
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#access-grant-endpoint
    traits: [Post, Delete, Get, AccessGrants, Public]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/access-endpoints-get-post-delete
    steps:
      - label: make the test container public (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.AccessGrantService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            type: [AccessGrant]
            storage: "${storage}"
            access:
              - type: [AccessPolicy]
                action: [read]
                assignee: http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/Agent
                target:
                  type: StorageResource
                  value: ["${test.container}"]
        response:
          statusCode: 201
          location:
            capture: grant
            cleanup: true
      - label: anyone can read it now
        as: anonymous
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${test.container}"
          accept: application/lws+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
      - label: revoke the grant
        request:
          method: DELETE
          url: "${grant}"
        response:
          statusCode: [200, 204]
      - label: anonymous reads are refused again
        as: anonymous
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${test.container}"
          accept: application/lws+json
        response:
          statusCode: 401

  - id: "#getContainer-public-read"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: getContainer-public-read
    label: A container granted to the public can be read without credentials
    comment: >-
      lws-test-suite's getContainer declares a public container as a prerequisite, which is
      right, but gives no way to realise it. Here the engine makes it public through the one
      mechanism the draft defines, an AccessGrant whose assignee is foaf:Agent (EXECUTION.md
      section 4.3). A target whose grant service refuses makes the test inapplicable.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#odrl-assignee
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#access-requests-and-grants
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#read-resource
    traits: [Get, Container, Public, AccessGrants]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/policy-assignee-uri-foaf-agent
    mirrors: lws10/manifest.jsonld#getContainer
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - container: notes
          authorization:
            read: [anonymous]
    as: anonymous
    request:
      method: GET
      url: "${notes}"
      accept: application/lws+json
    response:
      statusCode: 200
      contentType: application/lws+json
      json:
        - pointer: /type
          hasValue: Container

  - id: "#readDataResource-public-read"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: readDataResource-public-read
    label: A data resource granted to the public can be read without credentials
    comment: >-
      The public-read half of lws-test-suite's readDataResource. The grant targets the
      data resource itself, because the draft does not say whether a grant on a container
      reaches what it contains.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#odrl-assignee
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#odrl-target
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#read-resource
    traits: [Get, DataResource, Public, AccessGrants]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/policy-assignee-uri-foaf-agent
    mirrors: lws10/manifest.jsonld#readDataResource
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - dataResource: created
          contentType: text/plain
          bodyURL: ../fixtures/shoppinglist.txt
          authorization:
            read: [anonymous]
    as: anonymous
    request:
      method: GET
      url: "${created}"
    response:
      statusCode: 200
      contentType: text/plain
      bodyURL: ../fixtures/shoppinglist.txt

  - id: "#access-grant-authenticated-agent"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: access-grant-authenticated-agent
    label: A read grant to one agent lets that agent read, and no more
    comment: >-
      The authenticated-agent case lws-test-suite named Role-Authenticated and never
      used. bob gets read on one resource: he can read it, cannot replace it, and an
      anonymous client still cannot read it.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#odrl-action
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#odrl-assignee
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#access-requests-and-grants
    traits: [Get, Put, DataResource, AccessGrants, Authz]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/policy-action-values
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/authz-policy-denial-rejected
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - dataResource: created
          contentType: text/plain
          body: shared with bob, read-only
          authorization:
            read: [bob]
    steps:
      - label: bob can read it
        as: bob
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${created}"
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          bodyMatches: '^shared with bob, read-only$'
      - label: bob cannot replace it
        as: bob
        request:
          method: PUT
          url: "${created}"
          contentType: text/plain
          body: bob was here
        response:
          statusCode: [403, 404]
      - label: and it is still not public
        as: anonymous
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${created}"
        response:
          statusCode: 401


  - id: "#access-grant-extra-properties-accepted"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: access-grant-extra-properties-accepted
    label: A grant with an extra property, and without the optional inbox and constraint, is accepted and takes effect
    comment: >-
      "Other properties MAY be present on access requests and access grants", and inbox
      and constraint are OPTIONAL. A server that refuses a grant because it carries a
      property the server does not know, or lacks one it does not need, rejects a
      conforming document. The grant must also take effect: bob can then read what it
      names.
    status: Proposed
    level: MAY
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#access-data-model
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#access-inbox-property
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#odrl-constraint
    traits: [Post, Get, DataResource, AccessGrants, Authz]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/access-extra-properties-allowed
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/access-inbox-optional
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/policy-constraint-optional
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - dataResource: created
          contentType: text/plain
          body: shared by a grant with an extra property
    steps:
      - label: grant bob read access, with a property this specification does not define
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.AccessGrantService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            type: [AccessGrant]
            storage: "${storage}"
            "urn:touchstone:note": granted by the Touchstone conformance suite
            access:
              - type: [AccessPolicy]
                action: [read]
                assignee: "${identity.bob.webid}"
                target:
                  type: StorageResource
                  value: ["${created}"]
        response:
          statusCode: 201
          location:
            capture: grant
            cleanup: true
      - label: the grant takes effect
        as: bob
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${created}"
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          bodyMatches: '^shared by a grant with an extra property$'

  - id: "#access-grant-inbox-notified"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: access-grant-inbox-notified
    label: A grant with an inbox is announced there
    comment: >-
      "When an inbox property is present on an access request or access grant, the server
      SHOULD deliver notifications to that endpoint." alice grants bob read and names this
      test's inbox; a Notification must arrive there, conforming to the notification data
      model ("Notification serialization MUST conform").
    status: Proposed
    level: SHOULD
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#access-notifications
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#access-notification-events
    traits: [Post, Get, AccessGrants, Notifications]
    requires: [Authentication, ReachableFixtures]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/access-inbox-notifications
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/access-notification-events
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/access-notification-data-model
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/access-notification-delivery
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - dataResource: shared
          contentType: text/plain
          body: shared with bob
    steps:
      - label: grant bob read, naming this test's inbox
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.AccessGrantService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            type: [AccessGrant]
            storage: "${storage}"
            inbox: "${test.inbox}"
            access:
              - type: [AccessPolicy]
                action: [read]
                assignee: "${identity.bob.webid}"
                target:
                  type: StorageResource
                  value: ["${shared}"]
        response:
          statusCode: 201
          location:
            capture: grant
            cleanup: true
      - label: a Notification arrives at the inbox
        as: anonymous
        poll: {within: 30, every: 2}
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${test.inbox}"
          accept: application/json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /deliveries
              some:
                - pointer: /body/type
                  equals: Notification
                - pointer: /activities
                  some:
                    - pointer: /id
                      jsonType: string
                    - pointer: /type
                      jsonType: array
                    - pointer: /published
                      jsonType: string

  - id: "#access-request-create"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: access-request-create
    label: An agent submits an access request with POST
    comment: >-
      "An agent creates an access request by submitting a POST request to the access
      request endpoint", and a successful POST answers with Location. The storage
      controller can then read the request.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#access-protocol
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#access-data-model
    traits: [Post, Get, AccessGrants]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/access-post-location-header
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/access-type-values
    steps:
      - label: bob asks for read access to the test container
        as: bob
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.AccessRequestService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            type: [AccessRequest]
            storage: "${storage}"
            access:
              - type: [AccessPolicy]
                action: [read]
                assignee: "${identity.bob.webid}"
                target:
                  type: StorageResource
                  value: ["${test.container}"]
        response:
          statusCode: 201
          location:
            capture: accessRequest
            cleanup: true
      - label: the storage controller sees an AccessRequest
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${accessRequest}"
          accept: application/lws+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /type
              hasValue: AccessRequest

  - id: "#access-grant-document-shape"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: access-grant-document-shape
    label: An access grant reads back in the access data model, with every required property
    comment: >-
      access-grant-create checks the type, the storage and that access is an array. This
      checks the rest of the model a stored grant must keep: an @context ordered set including
      the LWS context, and an access collection whose every policy has a type including
      AccessPolicy, an action collection, an assignee and a target object with a type and a
      value collection.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#json-ld-serialization
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#access-property
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#odrl-type
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#odrl-target
    traits: [Post, Get, AccessGrants]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/access-jsonld-context-lws-v1
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/access-type-required
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/access-storage-required
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/access-access-required
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/access-access-collection
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/policy-type-required
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/policy-type-access-policy
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/policy-action-required
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/policy-assignee-required
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/policy-target-object
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - dataResource: created
          contentType: text/plain
          body: the target of a grant
    steps:
      - label: grant bob read access to it
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.AccessGrantService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            type: [AccessGrant]
            storage: "${storage}"
            access:
              - type: [AccessPolicy]
                action: [read]
                assignee: "${identity.bob.webid}"
                target:
                  type: StorageResource
                  value: ["${created}"]
        response:
          statusCode: 201
          location:
            capture: grant
            cleanup: true
      - label: the grant reads back in the access data model
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${grant}"
          accept: application/lws+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /@context
              jsonType: array
            - pointer: /@context
              hasValue: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1
            - pointer: /type
              hasValue: AccessGrant
            - pointer: /storage
              equalsIri: "${storage}"
            - pointer: /access
              jsonType: array
            - pointer: /access
              some:
                - pointer: /assignee
                  equalsIri: "${identity.bob.webid}"
            - pointer: /access
              every:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: AccessPolicy
                - pointer: /action
                  jsonType: array
                - pointer: /assignee
                  jsonType: string
                - pointer: /target
                  jsonType: object
                - pointer: /target/type
                  jsonType: string
                - pointer: /target/value
                  jsonType: array

  - id: "#access-grant-incomplete-refused"
    type: NegativeTest
    name: access-grant-incomplete-refused
    label: An access grant missing a required property, or with a malformed one, is refused and grants nothing
    comment: >-
      The draft makes type, storage and access REQUIRED on a grant, and type, action and
      assignee REQUIRED on each policy, and constrains their values, but says nothing of the
      response to a document that breaks them. A server that accepted one would then serve
      a grant that does not conform, so refusing it is the only conforming outcome (D-0060).
      Each defective grant would otherwise give bob read access; after them all, bob still
      has none. A complete grant then does give it, which shows the refusals were not just
      a server that grants nothing.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#access-type-property
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#access-storage-property
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#access-inbox-property
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#access-property
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#odrl-type
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#odrl-action
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#odrl-assignee
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#odrl-target
    traits: [Post, Get, AccessGrants, Authz]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/access-type-required
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/access-storage-required
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/access-access-required
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/access-access-collection
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/access-inbox-uri
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/policy-type-required
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/policy-type-access-policy
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/policy-action-required
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/policy-assignee-required
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/policy-target-object
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - dataResource: created
          contentType: text/plain
          body: not for bob
    steps:
      - label: a grant without its type is refused
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.AccessGrantService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            storage: "${storage}"
            access:
              - type: [AccessPolicy]
                action: [read]
                assignee: "${identity.bob.webid}"
                target:
                  type: StorageResource
                  value: ["${created}"]
        response:
          statusCode: "4xx"
      - label: a grant without storage is refused
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.AccessGrantService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            type: [AccessGrant]
            access:
              - type: [AccessPolicy]
                action: [read]
                assignee: "${identity.bob.webid}"
                target:
                  type: StorageResource
                  value: ["${created}"]
        response:
          statusCode: "4xx"
      - label: a grant without access is refused
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.AccessGrantService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            type: [AccessGrant]
            storage: "${storage}"
        response:
          statusCode: "4xx"
      - label: a grant whose access is empty is refused
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.AccessGrantService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            type: [AccessGrant]
            storage: "${storage}"
            access: []
        response:
          statusCode: "4xx"
      - label: a policy without its type is refused
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.AccessGrantService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            type: [AccessGrant]
            storage: "${storage}"
            access:
              - action: [read]
                assignee: "${identity.bob.webid}"
                target:
                  type: StorageResource
                  value: ["${created}"]
        response:
          statusCode: "4xx"
      - label: a policy whose type lacks AccessPolicy is refused
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.AccessGrantService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            type: [AccessGrant]
            storage: "${storage}"
            access:
              - type: ["urn:touchstone:not-an-access-policy"]
                action: [read]
                assignee: "${identity.bob.webid}"
                target:
                  type: StorageResource
                  value: ["${created}"]
        response:
          statusCode: "4xx"
      - label: a policy without action is refused
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.AccessGrantService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            type: [AccessGrant]
            storage: "${storage}"
            access:
              - type: [AccessPolicy]
                assignee: "${identity.bob.webid}"
                target:
                  type: StorageResource
                  value: ["${created}"]
        response:
          statusCode: "4xx"
      - label: a policy without assignee is refused
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.AccessGrantService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            type: [AccessGrant]
            storage: "${storage}"
            access:
              - type: [AccessPolicy]
                action: [read]
                target:
                  type: StorageResource
                  value: ["${created}"]
        response:
          statusCode: "4xx"
      - label: a policy whose target is not an object is refused
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.AccessGrantService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            type: [AccessGrant]
            storage: "${storage}"
            access:
              - type: [AccessPolicy]
                action: [read]
                assignee: "${identity.bob.webid}"
                target: "${created}"
        response:
          statusCode: "4xx"
      - label: a grant whose inbox is not a URI is refused
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.AccessGrantService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            type: [AccessGrant]
            storage: "${storage}"
            inbox: "not a uri"
            access:
              - type: [AccessPolicy]
                action: [read]
                assignee: "${identity.bob.webid}"
                target:
                  type: StorageResource
                  value: ["${created}"]
        response:
          statusCode: "4xx"
      - label: none of them gave bob access
        as: bob
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${created}"
        response:
          statusCode: [403, 404]
      - label: a complete grant is accepted
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.AccessGrantService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            type: [AccessGrant]
            storage: "${storage}"
            access:
              - type: [AccessPolicy]
                action: [read]
                assignee: "${identity.bob.webid}"
                target:
                  type: StorageResource
                  value: ["${created}"]
        response:
          statusCode: 201
          location:
            capture: grant
            cleanup: true
      - label: and does give bob access
        as: bob
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${created}"
        response:
          statusCode: 200

  - id: "#access-grant-constraints-all-satisfied"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: access-grant-constraints-all-satisfied
    label: A grant's constraints must all be satisfied before it permits access
    comment: >-
      "When multiple constraint objects are present, all of them MUST be satisfied." A grant
      to bob with two dateTime constraints, one met (on or after 2000-01-01) and one not (on
      or before 2000-01-02), must not let him read; a server treating the list as "any of"
      would. A second grant whose constraints are both met then must: that shows the server
      evaluates dateTime at all, rather than refusing everything constrained. Applies only
      where the grant service advertises the Access Profile, which is what obliges a server to
      support the dateTime leftOperand.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#odrl-constraint
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#constraint-combining
    traits: [Post, Get, AccessGrants, Authz]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/policy-constraints-all-satisfied
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/policy-constraints-conjunction-semantics
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/policy-constraint-left-operands
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/policy-constraint-objects
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - dataResource: created
          contentType: text/plain
          body: only within the window
    steps:
      - label: the grant service advertises the Access Profile (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: AccessGrantService
                - pointer: /conformsTo
                  hasValue: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws#AccessProfile
      - label: grant bob read, constrained to a window that has closed
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.AccessGrantService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            type: [AccessGrant]
            storage: "${storage}"
            access:
              - type: [AccessPolicy]
                action: [read]
                assignee: "${identity.bob.webid}"
                target:
                  type: StorageResource
                  value: ["${created}"]
                constraint:
                  - leftOperand: dateTime
                    operator: gteq
                    rightOperand: "2000-01-01T00:00:00Z"
                  - leftOperand: dateTime
                    operator: lteq
                    rightOperand: "2000-01-02T00:00:00Z"
        response:
          statusCode: 201
          location:
            capture: closed
            cleanup: true
      - label: one constraint met is not enough, so bob cannot read
        as: bob
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${created}"
        response:
          statusCode: [403, 404]
      - label: grant bob read again, constrained to a window that is open
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.AccessGrantService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            type: [AccessGrant]
            storage: "${storage}"
            access:
              - type: [AccessPolicy]
                action: [read]
                assignee: "${identity.bob.webid}"
                target:
                  type: StorageResource
                  value: ["${created}"]
                constraint:
                  - leftOperand: dateTime
                    operator: gteq
                    rightOperand: "2000-01-01T00:00:00Z"
                  - leftOperand: dateTime
                    operator: lteq
                    rightOperand: "2999-12-31T23:59:59Z"
        response:
          statusCode: 201
          location:
            capture: open
            cleanup: true
      - label: with both met, bob can read
        as: bob
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${created}"
        response:
          statusCode: 200

  - id: "#access-grant-left-operands-accepted"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: access-grant-left-operands-accepted
    label: A server advertising the Access Profile accepts a grant constrained by each leftOperand it must support
    comment: >-
      "A server advertising support for this profile MUST support the following
      leftOperand values": client, format, type, purpose and dateTime. A grant constrained
      by each one in turn, with the operator the draft's own example uses for it, must be
      accepted. A server that refuses one does not support it. Whether each is enforced is
      for the tests that follow; purpose has none, since the draft does not say how a
      request states its purpose.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#odrl-constraint
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#constraint-purpose
    traits: [Post, Get, AccessGrants, Authz]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/policy-constraint-left-operands
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/policy-constraint-objects
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - dataResource: created
          contentType: text/plain
          body: constrained five ways
    steps:
      - label: the grant service advertises the Access Profile (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: AccessGrantService
                - pointer: /conformsTo
                  hasValue: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws#AccessProfile
      - label: a client constraint is accepted
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.AccessGrantService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            type: [AccessGrant]
            storage: "${storage}"
            access:
              - type: [AccessPolicy]
                action: [read]
                assignee: "${identity.bob.webid}"
                target:
                  type: StorageResource
                  value: ["${created}"]
                constraint:
                  - leftOperand: client
                    operator: eq
                    rightOperand: urn:touchstone:client:conformance
        response:
          statusCode: 201
          location:
            capture: clientGrant
            cleanup: true
      - label: a format constraint is accepted
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.AccessGrantService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            type: [AccessGrant]
            storage: "${storage}"
            access:
              - type: [AccessPolicy]
                action: [read]
                assignee: "${identity.bob.webid}"
                target:
                  type: StorageResource
                  value: ["${created}"]
                constraint:
                  - leftOperand: format
                    operator: isAnyOf
                    rightOperand: [text/plain, application/json]
        response:
          statusCode: 201
          location:
            capture: formatGrant
            cleanup: true
      - label: a type constraint is accepted
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.AccessGrantService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            type: [AccessGrant]
            storage: "${storage}"
            access:
              - type: [AccessPolicy]
                action: [read]
                assignee: "${identity.bob.webid}"
                target:
                  type: StorageResource
                  value: ["${created}"]
                constraint:
                  - leftOperand: type
                    operator: eq
                    rightOperand: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws#DataResource
        response:
          statusCode: 201
          location:
            capture: typeGrant
            cleanup: true
      - label: a purpose constraint is accepted
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.AccessGrantService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            type: [AccessGrant]
            storage: "${storage}"
            access:
              - type: [AccessPolicy]
                action: [read]
                assignee: "${identity.bob.webid}"
                target:
                  type: StorageResource
                  value: ["${created}"]
                constraint:
                  - leftOperand: purpose
                    operator: isAnyOf
                    rightOperand: ["urn:touchstone:purpose:conformance-testing", "urn:touchstone:purpose:research"]
        response:
          statusCode: 201
          location:
            capture: purposeGrant
            cleanup: true
      - label: a dateTime constraint is accepted
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.AccessGrantService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            type: [AccessGrant]
            storage: "${storage}"
            access:
              - type: [AccessPolicy]
                action: [read]
                assignee: "${identity.bob.webid}"
                target:
                  type: StorageResource
                  value: ["${created}"]
                constraint:
                  - leftOperand: dateTime
                    operator: lteq
                    rightOperand: "2999-12-31T23:59:59Z"
        response:
          statusCode: 201
          location:
            capture: dateTimeGrant
            cleanup: true

  - id: "#access-grant-constraint-format"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: access-grant-constraint-format
    label: A format constraint lets a grant reach only resources of the listed media types
    comment: >-
      format represents "the media type of the target HTTP resource"; with isAnyOf, access
      is permitted if the resource's media type matches any listed value. One grant gives
      bob read on a text/plain and a text/csv resource, constrained to text/plain or
      application/json: he can read the first and not the second.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#odrl-constraint
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#constraint-format
    traits: [Post, Get, AccessGrants, Authz]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/policy-constraint-left-operands
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - dataResource: plain
          contentType: text/plain
          body: a listed media type
        - dataResource: csv
          contentType: text/csv
          body: "not,a,listed,media,type"
    steps:
      - label: the grant service advertises the Access Profile (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: AccessGrantService
                - pointer: /conformsTo
                  hasValue: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws#AccessProfile
      - label: grant bob read on both, for text/plain and application/json only
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.AccessGrantService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            type: [AccessGrant]
            storage: "${storage}"
            access:
              - type: [AccessPolicy]
                action: [read]
                assignee: "${identity.bob.webid}"
                target:
                  type: StorageResource
                  value: ["${plain}", "${csv}"]
                constraint:
                  - leftOperand: format
                    operator: isAnyOf
                    rightOperand: [text/plain, application/json]
        response:
          statusCode: 201
          location:
            capture: grant
            cleanup: true
      - label: bob can read the text/plain resource
        as: bob
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${plain}"
        response:
          statusCode: 200
      - label: but not the text/csv one
        as: bob
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${csv}"
        response:
          statusCode: [403, 404]

  - id: "#access-grant-constraint-type"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: access-grant-constraint-type
    label: A type constraint lets a grant reach only resources of the given type
    comment: >-
      type represents "the type URL expressed in a resource's link headers". One grant
      gives bob read on a container and a data resource, constrained to type eq
      lws#DataResource: he can read the data resource and not the container.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#odrl-constraint
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#constraint-type
    traits: [Post, Get, AccessGrants, Authz]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/policy-constraint-left-operands
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - container: box
        - dataResource: doc
          contentType: text/plain
          body: a data resource
    steps:
      - label: the grant service advertises the Access Profile (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: AccessGrantService
                - pointer: /conformsTo
                  hasValue: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws#AccessProfile
      - label: grant bob read on both, for data resources only
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.AccessGrantService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            type: [AccessGrant]
            storage: "${storage}"
            access:
              - type: [AccessPolicy]
                action: [read]
                assignee: "${identity.bob.webid}"
                target:
                  type: StorageResource
                  value: ["${box}", "${doc}"]
                constraint:
                  - leftOperand: type
                    operator: eq
                    rightOperand: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws#DataResource
        response:
          statusCode: 201
          location:
            capture: grant
            cleanup: true
      - label: bob can read the data resource
        as: bob
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${doc}"
        response:
          statusCode: 200
      - label: but not the container
        as: bob
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${box}"
        response:
          statusCode: [403, 404]

  - id: "#access-grant-constraint-client"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: access-grant-constraint-client
    label: A client constraint withholds a grant from every other client application
    comment: >-
      client represents "the client identifier for an HTTP request". A grant to bob
      limited to a client identifier his client does not have must not let him read. An
      unconstrained grant then must: that shows the refusal came from the constraint, not
      from bob.
    status: Proposed
    level: MUST
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#odrl-constraint
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#constraint-client
    traits: [Post, Get, AccessGrants, Authz]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/policy-constraint-left-operands
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - dataResource: created
          contentType: text/plain
          body: for one client application only
    steps:
      - label: the grant service advertises the Access Profile (otherwise this test does not apply)
        precondition: true
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${storage}"
          accept: application/lws+cid
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /service
              some:
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: AccessGrantService
                - pointer: /conformsTo
                  hasValue: https://www.w3.org/ns/lws#AccessProfile
      - label: grant bob read, for a client that is not his
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.AccessGrantService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            type: [AccessGrant]
            storage: "${storage}"
            access:
              - type: [AccessPolicy]
                action: [read]
                assignee: "${identity.bob.webid}"
                target:
                  type: StorageResource
                  value: ["${created}"]
                constraint:
                  - leftOperand: client
                    operator: eq
                    rightOperand: urn:touchstone:client:not-bobs
        response:
          statusCode: 201
          location:
            capture: constrained
            cleanup: true
      - label: bob's own client cannot read
        as: bob
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${created}"
        response:
          statusCode: [403, 404]
      - label: grant bob read without a constraint
        request:
          method: POST
          url: "${service.AccessGrantService}"
          contentType: application/lws+json
          bodyJSON:
            "@context": ["https://www.w3.org/ns/lws/v1"]
            type: [AccessGrant]
            storage: "${storage}"
            access:
              - type: [AccessPolicy]
                action: [read]
                assignee: "${identity.bob.webid}"
                target:
                  type: StorageResource
                  value: ["${created}"]
        response:
          statusCode: 201
          location:
            capture: unconstrained
            cleanup: true
      - label: now bob can read
        as: bob
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${created}"
        response:
          statusCode: 200

  - id: "#container-listing-filtered-metadata"
    type: ValidationTest
    name: container-listing-filtered-metadata
    label: A listing filtered by authorization still gives each member it shows its core metadata
    comment: >-
      "For containers, the server returns a listing of member resources which MAY be
      filtered based on authorization. Listings must include core metadata for each member."
      bob may read a container and one of its data resources but not the other. Whatever his
      listing shows, the member he may read among it, every member carries an id and a type,
      and the readable data resource its format. Omitting the member he may not read is the
      MAY; listing it is allowed too, with its metadata. A server where a grant on a container
      reaches its members simply shows him both.
    status: Proposed
    level: MAY
    source:
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#read-resource
      - https://www.w3.org/TR/2026/WD-lws10-core-20261005/#container-representation
    traits: [Get, Container, AccessGrants, Authz]
    requires: [Authentication]
    requirements:
      - https://example.org/touchstone/req/lws10-core/read-container-listing-authz-filtered
    prereqs:
      hierarchy:
        - container: box
          authorization:
            read: [bob]
        - dataResource: visible
          in: box
          contentType: text/plain
          body: bob may read this
          authorization:
            read: [bob]
        - dataResource: hidden
          in: box
          contentType: text/plain
          body: bob is granted nothing on this
    steps:
      - label: bob's listing shows the member he may read, and core metadata for every member it shows
        as: bob
        request:
          method: GET
          url: "${box}"
          accept: application/lws+json
        response:
          statusCode: 200
          json:
            - pointer: /items
              some:
                - pointer: /id
                  equalsIri: "${visible}"
                - pointer: /type
                  hasValue: DataResource
                - pointer: /format
                  jsonType: string
            - pointer: /items
              every:
                - pointer: /id
                  jsonType: string
                - pointer: /type
                  exists: true
